# Recommended fix chunk (out of scope for W44-34 investigate; queue for next chunk)
Chunk-type: dispatch-classifier refinement (analogous to entropy_mul smart_dispatch in
            content_aware_entropy_mul_ab.rs).
Mechanism: extend `adapt_to_image_lossy` with a content-aware override that re-enables
           try_dct64 when image smoothness predicts DCT64 wins. Possible features:
           - block-mean stddev (low = smooth = DCT64 wins)
           - high-frequency-energy ratio (low = smooth = DCT64 wins)
           - kurtosis or std-dev percentile
           Calibrate on a stratified set of 6-10 images across content classes (not just
           7256805) at d ∈ {0.5, 1.0, 1.5, 2.0} sweep.
Expected win: ~6 % bytes recovery on smooth-photo 512×512 cells (5 OPEN ledger entries),
              zero impact on non-smooth small images (verified by 7256805 baseline).
Risk: wall-clock cost. Forcing try_dct64=true on 1418519 added <2 ms/encode in this
      bench — within noise. The original W44-17 wall-clock rationale was speed of
      tiny_0.07MP and large_2.78MP cells, both of which would not flip under a
      smoothness gate (large_2.78MP keeps try_dct64=true via the pixel gate anyway).

